Hover events now feed the source model and authored view. The remaining
controller action graph, quantity backend, physical-item renderer and
selected-item factory lifecycle retain their existing admission guards.
This does not establish installed tooltip or input parity.

Retain selected-item detail factory creations independently of the bundle source and tooltip visibility. The verified state-52 cell helper requests the fixed popup_tip_text name with the supplied native child hover text and strict boolean exclusive=true only for a selected physical child. Deselection, padding and overflow leave existing details alone. Retire only the completed creation ID after animation traversal; late completion cannot remove its replacement. Include creation identity in component reconciliation to release old captures and toggle state.

The selected-cell helper remains behind the active bundle input/rendering admission boundary. The full controller graph, native visibility producer, complete child description formatter and installed visual comparison remain unfinished.

Render physical bundle item references from the same owned preview snapshot that built the scene. Reject missing, stale, empty, fractional and ambiguous references. Preserve full child counts and components; draw icons and native count labels independently of Java slots, quickcraft decorations and action dispatch. Reuse the authored item rectangle and per-extraction native opacity/filter style. Physical durability and storage controls retain the scene snapshot values.

A screen extraction regression draws count255 as99+ with authored scale and native filter state, restores the extraction transform/style, and preserves both the retained snapshot and Java menu. Sparse source-to-scene regressions retain holes and reject malformed references. Pinned native count producer141913620 covers536 complete strings; existing original bundle layout controls establish physical cell order. Active admission remains guarded pending the full action graph, description formatter, visibility source and installed native comparison.

Read inventory hover sources from the control event property bag instead of render-only collection/slot annotations. Preserve native typed defaults and integer narrowing, and retain live bag reads rather than copying a source when the event is created. Structural collection annotations still identify render slots.

Original Bedrock 1.26.60.5/protocol2225 input producer14192b090 retains the UIControl bag from141c3a4e0; source getter14500e920/140085b60 reads its string #collection_name. Eight native composition controls preserve heap strings, reject boolean values and observe replacement after enqueue. The collection_details initializer14191e310 and original ancestor lookup/enumeration populate #collection_index and prefixed variants, with fifteen execution controls. The shared program prerequisite now exports those final values. Local event regressions use a routed slot event, change its retained bag and reject structural fallback and invalid JSON types. Full inventory FSM and installed parity remain separate gates.

Route desktop player/workbench bundle activation through the optional typed
native_bundle_input channel. Use each callback's property-bag collection and
index; never derive command authority from renderer or Java slot ordinals.
Match the original 1.26.60.5 state1 controls for ordinary cursor insertion,
held-bundle insertion and default extraction. Empty-cursor secondary extraction
requires the retained hover tooltip mode2. Touch/retained-source gestures and
native sound/controller composition remain separate unfinished work.

Share the player presentation's monotonic sequence, result channel, timeout
and retirement rules across bundle and recipe/search commands. Queue search
edits during a bundle request and bind the next command to the latest received
publication. Consume handled pointer/keyboard events and their releases so Java
does not send an additional inventory action. Block physical player actions
while a native command is pending. Validate complete carried-bundle snapshots
instead of applying the previous blanket tooltip fallback on player screens.

Real exported-program pointer regressions exercise primary and secondary
inputs with roots on either the cursor or clicked inventory source, verify the
exact scoped payload, preserve local stacks, and reject a second pending click
without Java dispatch. Presentation regressions cover stale replies, revision
updates, shared sequencing, buffered search, timeout and retired openings.
Installed direct/proxy behavior, sound effects and full native parity remain
unverified by these Java tests.

Allow the implemented physical desktop hover view to refresh before input.
Disabled native tooltip controls clear their old hover without claiming the
pointer or requiring an action implementation. Geometry invalidation repeats
admission when enablement changes and still rejects enabled unsupported
controls. Regressions exercise a full exported tooltip refresh before all four
bundle gestures and prove that a disabled touch control cannot become active
without validation. Full installed pixels and native traversal remain unverified.

Validate complete physical player/workbench bundle snapshots during frame
extraction with the owned tooltip cache. Do not apply the obsolete blanket
storage guard after the source/controller path has admitted those snapshots.
Keep fallback for unsupported generic screens and recipe/ghost previews.

Route the filled-tooltip hide callback through retained source state.
Original 1.26.60.5 closure14503ba10 changes the hidden flag only for raw
profile2 and returns false for desktop profiles1/3. Admit tapped_bundle_item_icon
from bundle_items: original state52 consumes mode0/2 input without selection
changes. Retained mode1 detail input keeps its explicit fallback until native
description and lifetime production are established.

Frame-extraction tests retain an actual hovered bundle without retiring its
presentation. Exported-program extraction tests use filled physical previews,
refresh before input, check the desktop cell/hide callbacks, and move the
hovered bundle to the cursor before another refresh. GPU drawing, scissor
submission and item conversion are supplied services. Complete native pixels,
controller composition, touch and retained detail lifetimes remain unverified.

Play optional bundle operation results through the current accepted native
level-event library, sound banks and captions. Match the pending command's
opening, generation, request and input kind before playback. Duplicate,
unrelated and retired replies remain silent; legacy result codecs stay intact.

