sound and position helpers execute together in24 controls against executable
SHA-256988f6a61403b4381aa41e6c66d64cce441b14e561a9b10f647c2758ef3f2672a.
Admission/mutation and the final level virtual remain supplied. Client boundary
regressions cover reply lifetime, selected resources, captions and missing actors;
these checks do not establish installed audio or exact native timing.

Reconcile retained bundle hover after model changes instead of requiring a
new pointer edge. Native1.26.60.5 getter144cd9340 and update blocks
145007eb6..145007f37/145008f40..1450090d2 execute72 repeated availability
updates across desktop, touch and gamepad profiles with inline/heap sources.
Desktop/gamepad restore mode2 from the retained hover; touch does not.
Initial invalidation preserves the independent primary selection.

Keep physical pointer hover while serialized item commands block button
actions, including repeated clicks awaiting a reply. Real screen regressions
reproduce the former manufactured pointer leave and require source restoration
without sending another item command. Unchanged hover does not rebuild scenes.
Storage admission and intervening native controller/model work remain explicit
probe boundaries; these controls do not establish complete controller parity.

Guard resize and GUI-scale rebuilds with the same ordinary-menu fallback
used for live presentation updates. A retired presentation can be observed
before its next tick cleanup; rebuilding it must not escape through
Screen.resize. Retain the connection and exact menu guard so fallback
preserves the cursor and cannot restore a menu that has already changed.
A full-screen resize regression covers both ownership outcomes.

Initialize the installed container hover with separate physical X and Y
input conversions from the shared viewport. Java rounds each GUI dimension
independently; drawing scale is not its input inverse on odd frame sizes.
Keep the initial hover aligned with subsequent pointer and extraction events.

Route desktop drop keys through the authored input router, including their
matching releases. Native Bedrock 1.26.60.5 bindings admit recipe/catalog
and actual slot controls; panels and outside areas do not handle these
sources. Drop-one prefers the carried stack. Drop-all requires an empty
cursor before targeting a real slot. Retain the source chosen on press
until release to preserve modifier order and one action per hold. Keep
search, close, ownership and pending-command admission intact.

Bind supported cooking search editors to an optional snapshot-owned core
query channel. Coalesce raw edits while recipe input or a prior query
remains pending, share monotonic request ordering, and retain newer text
when older snapshots and acknowledgments arrive. Keep one editor across
resize and retire the opening on ambiguous sends, timeout, or capability
withdrawal. Unknown controls still retain the ordinary Java screen.

Official Bedrock 1.26.60.5 integrated-world desktop controls retain
furnace search through category switches and reopening, independently
of smoker search. Client regressions cover queued edits, gesture release,
request ordering, stale replies, timeout, typing, resize, and fallback.
These controls do not establish complete default cooking admission,
installed direct/proxy delivery, other devices, or complete pixels.

Retain the newest local cooking edit or explicit clear in the connection
until disconnect. A menu that closes before a reply or query flush
restores this intent under the next opening's own identity and sequence.
Late results cannot release that replacement opening. Keep the query
response deadline active until both its acknowledgment and newer source
snapshot arrive, so a missing publication cannot leave inert controls.

Retain the original ordinary menu screen across native presentation replacements.
A rejected replacement retires the currently displayed native presentation,
and a later render failure restores that same ordinary host rather than a
closed native renderer. Keep the real menu, carried stack, slots and packet
ownership intact during recovery.

Bind the native cooking editor through its retained property name and
selection mappings. Only its own embedded clear control can clear the
field; it blocks covered inventory slots. Keep the local query visible
while an older edit waits for a reply without replacing recipe authority.

Bedrock 1.26.60.5 desktop controls show that embedded X clears during an
active input lifetime and preserves typing, including after the first
Escape. A reopened inactive field keeps its retained text when X is
clicked. Whitespace still shows X. Screen regressions use the exported
native editor and cover these paths while a query is pending. Complete
default cooking host bindings and installed-route parity remain open.

Keep the parsed player inventory program for repeated snapshots whose complete
authored bytes are unchanged. Snapshot revision and source data can change
without replacing resources; reparsing the entire scene graph on each update
adds avoidable client-thread allocation and decoding. Changed program bytes
still replace the resolver, and the cache belongs only to one presentation.
Retain search, collection and preview updates independently of this resource
lifetime. Regression coverage keeps authored label replacement and malformed
update rejection independent of retained query state.
Decode the incoming snapshot once per accepted update and compare against the
already retained state. Pass that state through replacement so family checks,
selection retirement and publication cannot independently repeat JSON decoding.

Bind the current native layout increment/decrement callbacks through the
same authored event router as tab navigation. Publish the current tab,
filter and changed layout independently of controller-local retained-tab
state. Forced recipe-book layouts consume the input without a change.

Current 1.26.60.5 registration tables identify both action hashes and
original callback execution establishes their transition rules. Screen
regressions preserve a carried stack, suppress held duplicates, and wait
for the matching profile snapshot across screen, panel and button hosts.
Other default cooking host actions and installed route parity remain open.

Dispatch authored cursor-drop actions through the shared component event
path for player and cooking screens. Pointer input must reach the same
ordinary inventory request owner as keyboard input, exactly once per press.
Keep empty cursors, pending commands and Help transitions silent. Partial
container scopes retain ordinary screens when they require cursor drops.

Official 1.26.60.5 player and furnace desktop controls retain nine ingots
through a blank-panel click, drop one on secondary input, and drop the
remainder on primary input. An 800-millisecond secondary hold acts once.
Screen regressions cover both buttons, keyboard delivery without a duplicate
request, empty/pending cursors and the transition into Help. Other common
source-reset handlers and full default cooking admission remain unfinished.
